 ## Ownership map
 
+Live BTW keeps one logical root session.
+Plugin storage owns the current native transcript ID and reservation.
+Root metadata contains a copy for the native interface.
+`lib/liveBtw.ts` admits snapshots prepared through the adapter and the BTW coordinator plugin.
+The coordinator publishes the head only after the adapter imports and materializes the snapshot.
+The existing-session send path uses the prepared transcript before optimistic insertion and prompt admission.
+The server holds a root reservation through admission across all clients.
+The native panel follows the root's head without changing the selected main session.
+Preparation loads the imported transcript through the shared message loader before publishing that head.
+An optimistic new question must not make an unmaterialized import appear complete.
+The live composer keeps drafts on the logical root while its execution transcript changes.
+Selection insertion addresses the column mailbox, which uses the live root or the ordinary session ID.
+Undo restores text, attachments and context to that root on every runtime.
+The native revert and its rollback still address the execution transcript.
+`revert-composer.ts` captures and restores the root's input if the native revert fails.
+Consumed context returns only after a failed send.
+Live imports retain their native transcript order through the server and event sequence.
+The host preserves that sequence without sorting replayed questions by their original dates.
+Newly admitted messages follow the imported block.
+Original message timestamps remain available for display.
+
+Queue delivery uses `hasActiveSubagent` with an explicit parent resolver over
+the cached sync session index. This keeps the 8-level ancestor walk shared
+with display activity while leaving the global display resolver unchanged.
 The VS Code queue gate and its live inputs are documented in
 `../stores/DOCUMENTATION.md`.
 
